{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world","id":1220967,"title":"[Dark Eras] How Orders Conquared the World?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-21T15:17:08-07:00","id":1220967,"title":"[Dark Eras] How Orders Conquared the World?","content":"So we had a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220900#post1220900\">big discussion in Werewolf forum if Diamond Orders should simply be <i>anywhere</i></a> on globe, once <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">created (probably) in Ancient Rome</a>. On one hand, Arcana can let mages do (almost) anything so any Awakened can go whenever you want it, spreading Orders ideas. On the other hand, we have evidence in <i>Princes of Conquated Land</i> in <b>Dark Eras Companion</b> - or material in 1E corebook on Boston mages - that Atlantis Orders where <b>not</b> directly connected all over the world once Orders come to being and it was more a process of spread for those ideas. More, in Mutapa Empire from <i>Princes</i> Era Europeans brought proper Orders with them only in 15th century AD - native mages follows only their Darshanas cults versions, not Orders hailing from Greco-Roman times.<br /> <br /> And now we have real dillemma - <b>Should Norse mages at the dawn of Vikings Era have any Orders in their society? </b>Norseman, as people, are part of migration of Germanic people from 1st century that was 'stucked' on the North. There are evidence there was small, but real trade, from time to time with continent. Would this be enough for Atlantean Orders to 'take whole North', going from Rome, by Germanic barbarians, to the Norse? Even when contact of Norseman with continent was almost non-existing?<br /> <br /> <b>I <i>think</i> answer should be 'No', as other way around it would mean that Diamond Order long before reached and converted Mutapa Empire than Dark Eras canon described first contact of 15th century AD</b> - as Ancient Rome have coastal Africa colonies in Empire times ( 1st century BCE - 4th century AD ), so in 500 years they should conquered whole Africa if we go with reasoning 'mages can do anything and surely they spread Orders further and further'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2018, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:46:02-07:00","id":1220977,"title":"","content":"I think your understanding of how the Orders spread is wrong. The Orders didn't conquer, they were simply more mobile and easily syncretized into as many local Mage customs as possible. As has been pointed out more than once, Mages don't typically fight each other violently because that's a really good way to end up in the Mage equivalent of a nuclear war. So the more likely course of action is cautious diplomacy, an exchange of ideas, some level of syncretism as common ground is found, and then these two groups decide they're in essentially the same magical tribe, an Order as they call it. That just keeps happening over and over again, and really it since it's not conquest it only needs a very tenuous level of connection, and as you've noted Mages can do pretty much anything so once a connection is established to anywhere, there will be communication across any distance. Not even in terms of Space magic, since the Astral also conveniently provides entire realms to meet and communicate in without going anywhere physically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:49:37-07:00","id":1220979,"title":"","content":"^ All of that ^<br /> <br /> Even the use of the word conquered makes me feel like you POV is skewed. If that works for your table, that\u2019s perfectly fine, but don\u2019t expect textual support in future books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:57:57-07:00","id":1220983,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I just checked out the other thread this one spawned and feel a bit bad for even responding, the people over there did a fine job of answering your questions and you just refused to believe them, and now the same thing is just going to happen over here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:06:45-07:00","id":1220986,"title":"","content":"It's the circle of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:11:51-07:00","id":1220987,"title":"","content":"Culturally-localized Orders conquering or fighting with each other is more of an Ascension thing, Wyrd. And even there Mages from distant places had plenty of ways to communicate, but in the classic World of Darkness everyone's at least a bit of a jerk.<br /> <br /> In Awakening, it's as it has been pointed out, with mages with resonant ideas realizing that their point of view is similar enough to justify an association. Cultural flavor is there, of course, but if two Awakened cultures interact for long enough, their members will soon realize who shares their beliefs and could be an ally. Then syncretism, common grounds and years of collaboration, until one day they all agree it was all part of the same Order. Cultural clashes aren't really something that has a cause within the Diamond Orders themselves, but rather within more mundane cultural differences or personal perspectives.<br /> <br /> As for why Mages from all over the world would want to explore and push the boundaries of the known world in a way that allows them to get in contact with others way before their respective mortal societies would...well, that's because they're Mages. Those curious nerds are never satisfied.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And now I checked it too and feel kinda dumb. Seriously Wyrd, if you don't like the answers people give you and have in mind something you feel would work better at your table or you enjoy more/believe makes more sense for your story, it's<i> fine</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-21-2018, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:26:17-07:00","id":1220988,"title":"","content":"Okay, so- <br /> <br /> * reads other posts again<br /> <br /> All that needs to be said has been said, it seems. <br /> <br /> So changing the perspective a little bit: if any of the Orders do some active conquering over integrating, it\u2019d be the Seers.<br /> <br /> Yes, this loops back to the original issue at hand since the Seers didn\u2019t properly form until relatively recently, but I\u2019m imagining proto-Seer cults subverting honest belief in local gods to self-enslavement to the Tyrants.<br /> <br /> Another perspective: the Tremere are said to have explicitly devoured Reaper Legacies all over the world, so there\u2019s an element of conquering there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:30:27-07:00","id":1220990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1220988#post1220988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So changing the perspective a little bit: if any of the Orders do some active conquering over integrating, it\u2019d be the Seers.<br /> <br /> Yes, this loops back to the original issue at hand since the Seers didn\u2019t properly form until relatively recently, but I\u2019m imagining proto-Seer cults subverting honest belief in local gods to self-enslavement to the Tyrants.<br /> <br /> Another perspective: the Tremere are said to have explicitly devoured Reaper Legacies all over the world, so there\u2019s an element of conquering there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, in my reply I totally forgot about Seers and Tremere. Talk about tunnel vision.<br /> <br /> Thanks for bringing them into the discussion, good points are being made there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:39:16-07:00","id":1220991,"title":"","content":"I do want to bring up a point in regards to the Hamster meta-discussion to simply point out that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067712#post1067712\">it's really not like this shit hasn't been explained before.</a><br /> <br /> Adding my voice to the chorus of &quot;If that's how you want to do it, just do it&quot;. You have got to stop wasting our time by asking us things and then ignoring us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-21-2018, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:43:31-07:00","id":1220992,"title":"","content":"Also an excellent point as to why framing the Diamond as conquerors doesn't fit. Really Wyrd, you are super focused on th supremacy of Euro-Roman orders, but unlike pretty much every other splat this doesn't make sense in Mage. Mages are capable of globalizing, so the Orders are global phenomenon that have been interpreted locally.<br /> <br /> Everyone loves to talk about wars in history, but you'll be hard pressed to find a historian who won't argue trade is more important. Same thing here,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:46:31-07:00","id":1220993,"title":"","content":"Seriously. The dominance of the main sects has less to do with RAWR RAWR and more to do with &quot;HOLY SHIT, THESE GUYS HAVE THE LIMITED EDITION LIGHTSABERS, IT'S SO COOL YOU GUYS.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:48:36-07:00","id":1220994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1220993#post1220993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously. The dominance of the main sects has less to do with RAWR RAWR and more to do with &quot;HOLY SHIT, THESE GUYS HAVE THE LIMITED EDITION LIGHTSABERS, IT'S SO COOL YOU GUYS.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That seriously cracked me up, just amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:49:38-07:00","id":1220995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1220994#post1220994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seriously cracked me up, just amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:56:01-07:00","id":1220997,"title":"","content":"I don't know what happened in the other thread, but I'm confused by what Wyrdhamster is asking this time? If they don't want the Orders to have reached Scandinavia at that time then...then that's that...?<br /> <br /> The Orders, though, didn't go around proselytizing their ideas. The Orders <i>exist</i> because different cultures of Mages met and exchanged ideas. They didn't then go around preaching Diamond ideals, but when they reached a new culture they were able to say, &quot;Yeah, we understand everything you're talking about and have libraries and warehouses full of Artifacts. Let's share ideas.&quot;<br /> <br /> That...was the whole point of To the Strongest, wasn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T16:58:33-07:00","id":1220998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1220997#post1220997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what happened in the other thread, but I'm confused by what Wyrdhamster is asking this time? If they don't want the Orders to have reached Scandinavia at that time then...then that's that...?<br /> <br /> The Orders, though, didn't go around proselytizing their ideas. The Orders <i>exist</i> because different cultures of Mages met and exchanged ideas. They didn't then go around preaching Diamond ideals, but when they reached a new culture they were able to say, &quot;Yeah, we understand everything you're talking about and have libraries and warehouses full of Artifacts. Let's share ideas.&quot;<br /> <br /> That...was the whole point of To the Strongest, wasn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Summed up in one. The only thing missing is that Hamster disbelieves that Scandinavia would have gotten in contact with the Diamond Orders or Exarch Cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-21-2018, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:06:12-07:00","id":1220999,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think Scandinavia was as cut off from rest of Europe as Wyrd believes. And even if regular Scandinavians were, mages were not. Their capabilities makes them perfect explorers, and their obsessions is a perfect drive for their exploration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Their/they're 05-21-2018, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:55:37-07:00","id":1221009,"title":"","content":"Well if they don't want the Orders in Norse Scandinavia then just do that. They don't need our permission, and Canon Cops aren't going to bust down their front door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T18:27:09-07:00","id":1221016,"title":"","content":"Look at it this way. You\u2019ve got magic, yeah? You touched infinity and saw the world the way it should be. And now you\u2019ve got to figure out a way to live with it without breaking the minds of everyone around you and/or summoning up an abomination from the deep places.<br /> <br /> You could try to make yourself a finer man. To hone your sword-arm and use your magic to be yourself, but more. And if you were to run into some Byzantine cavalryman with a tattoo of arrows hidden on his arm, you\u2019d recognize him as a brother.<br /> <br /> You could witness something called up that cannot be put down, a shrieking thing of bones and skin. It opens your eyes; you need to be careful, and you need to keep your gift from hurting others (and to stop things like that from doing the same). And if you were to run into some Briton who speaks of labyrinths, you would understand his meaning.<br /> <br /> You could go out and gather the secret and hidden things of the world, and follow wherever they point you, and when you come across a monastery with a second library, one opened by a word in no earthly tongue, you would embrace the Christian who keeps the mysteries safe.<br /> <br /> Or you could seek to use your power to make men wiser, to make yourself a jarl, to point men towards the enlightenment you\u2019ve seen. Maybe you think of it as climbing the world tree, but the symbol of the climb- that is universal.<br /> <br /> One improvement I\u2019ve seen in Mage 2e moving forward is the idea that the Diamond Orders aren\u2019t Proto-Atlantean-High-Secrets but, rather, groups of likeminded people that coalesce around the same symbols and ideals, and eventually retrofit the idea of Atlantis to explain these very human drives when faced with the gift of enlightenment: self-improvement, secrecy, study, and leadership. And when you meet someone from a foreign sect, those similarities will be more important than the regional differences.<br /> <br /> Also them Vikings were all over the Mediterranean, you know what I mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T18:37:02-07:00","id":1221020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raz_Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221016#post1221016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One improvement I\u2019ve seen in Mage 2e moving forward is the idea that <b>the Diamond Orders aren\u2019t Proto-Atlantean-High-Secrets</b> but, rather, groups of likeminded people that coalesce around the same symbols and ideals, and eventually retrofit the idea of Atlantis to explain these very human drives when faced with the gift of enlightenment<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This, basically. Emphasis mine. <br /> <br /> This also ties in to those recent threads<br /> we had earlier about \u201cLiches are only taboo because the \u2018Atlantean paradigm\u2019 says so\u201d and \u201cthe Supernal is just what the mainstream says.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T21:55:25-07:00","id":1221069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raz_Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221016#post1221016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One improvement I\u2019ve seen in Mage 2e moving forward is the <b>idea that the Diamond Orders aren\u2019t Proto-Atlantean-High-Secrets</b> but, rather, groups of likeminded people that coalesce around the same symbols and ideals, and eventually retrofit the idea of Atlantis to explain these very human drives when faced with the gift of enlightenment: self-improvement, secrecy, study, and leadership. And when you meet someone from a foreign sect, those similarities will be more important than the regional differences.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>And here is our main point of disagreement - to me, (Atlantean) Orders ARE those Greeco-Roman ( with mix of Hindu ) organisations. </b>Atlantis maybe ( or not ) a largest secret, but the Orders-as-Organisations are based on those Greeco-Roman roots. They have clear dogmas ( Silver Ladder in their name, Five Phalanx of Arrows or Diamond Wheel of Guardians ) with <i>a lot</i> of Greeco-Roman titles. To say that you are member one of Diamond Order you need to point that you are local Epopt, Cultor or Adamntine Sage. <b>Those are NOT original concepts from, for example, Norse culture traditions.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I do not question the existence of Darshans Cults around the world - it's just the fact of 2E Mage. All over the globe, every culture has it's warriors-mages, priest-mages, assassins-mages and scholars-mages.</b> It's a 2E gameline fact, shown in <i>To the Strongest</i> and <i>Princes of Conquered Land </i>Era.<b> I only point that each Darshanas Cults have it's own 'native flavor' and may not agree with joining Diamond Orders coalition on just seeing them</b> - and those Cults can just want to stay 'Nameless' longer - just like we see in <i>Princes of Conquered Lands</i> Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raz_Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221016#post1221016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also them Vikings were all over the Mediterranean, you know what I mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFTER the start of Viking Age ( circa 800 AD ) they were over Mediterranean - before they at most went to Germania to trade a bit with neighbors. And I question that those Germans they encountered were 'Atlantean' enough to the spread of Orders on global scale as fast you propose here. I much more envision that North Germans would still be as 'non-Atlantean' as Norse on the North, with maybe some individuals agreeing and joining proper Diamond Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2018, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:03:56-07:00","id":1221072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221069#post1221069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here is our main point of disagreement - to me, (Atlantean) Orders ARE those Greeco-Roman ( with mix of Hindu ) organisations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stopping you here, because this is not a thing you can disagree on. You are just straight up, flat out, empirically <i>wrong </i>if this is how you read it, and any further insistence on this train of thought had better reclassify itself as homebrew real quick before it becomes a bad faith argument.<br /> <br /> Also, seriously, Darshana is a localized, temporally fixed concept. It is a thing that applied pretty strictly to the To The Strongest setting. Please stop mis-using the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-22-2018, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:16:10-07:00","id":1221074,"title":"","content":"I'm actually curious, how are you defining Graeco-Roman in something like To the Strongest. This is definitely the Graeco portion of it, what with Alexander III having just recently passed away at the outset of the setting. However, the Romans don't turn up until, something like 200yrs later if memory serves. There's also the fact that all the Darshanas seem to originate in the Indian subcontinent based on their names and the fact that only one of the cults is actually of Greek origin. The orders aren't some form of Ancient mage Colonialism from my reading at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:24:43-07:00","id":1221075,"title":"","content":"Actually, sorry for the double post, I was just thinking. You know what would probably get some answers that would help more. Rather than saying &quot;Why are the colonial mages wrecking up my Norse setting?&quot;, why not ask something more along the lines of &quot;In my game I'm planning on having several nameless orders populating the Scandinavian regions cira. XXXX, does anyone have some cool ideas on what they could be?&quot;. One makes people check the books and question how you're getting this from material that doesn't explain things the way you're talking about them, the other would hopefully get some creative juices flowing about things like how Seidr practitioners might be treated, how male mages would be considered Ergi etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:59:03-07:00","id":1221084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221075#post1221075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, sorry for the double post, I was just thinking. You know what would probably get some answers that would help more. Rather than saying &quot;Why are the colonial mages wrecking up my Norse setting?&quot;, why not ask something more along the lines of &quot;In my game I'm planning on having several nameless orders populating the Scandinavian regions cira. XXXX, does anyone have some cool ideas on what they could be?&quot;. One makes people check the books and question how you're getting this from material that doesn't explain things the way you're talking about them, the other would hopefully get some creative juices flowing about things like how Seidr practitioners might be treated, how male mages would be considered Ergi etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone should Seidmadr and get on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-22-2018, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T23:45:01-07:00","id":1221091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221074#post1221074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually curious, how are you defining Graeco-Roman in something like To the Strongest. This is definitely the Graeco portion of it, what with Alexander III having just recently passed away at the outset of the setting. However, the Romans don't turn up until, something like 200yrs later if memory serves. There's also the fact that all the Darshanas seem to originate in the Indian subcontinent based on their names and the fact that only one of the cults is actually of Greek origin. The orders aren't some form of Ancient mage Colonialism from my reading at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">Roman part is suspected only, based on vague hints in books, it's true</a>. Rome, as city-state, existed at least from 753 BC and was active in Mediterranean Sea from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Rome#Punic_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Punic Wars</a> onward, from 264 BC. And a lot of Latin names of titles in Order points that some reform in Rome was in making.<br /> <br /> However, <i>To The Strongest</i> points you have both Indian and Greek names for Darshanas - and that Greek mages use rather their own names for Schools ( See Dark Eras 1, page 86-90. Darshanas is global phenomena, showing itself again and again all the time - but first <i>named</i> time in Alexander times, in India, and then term goes to Greek mages.<ul><li>Jnanashakti = Gnostikon</li> <li>Samashti = Phulakeion</li> <li>Vajrasta = Adamantine Arrow</li> <li>Mahanizrayani = Omphalos</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221075#post1221075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what would probably get some answers that would help more. Rather than saying &quot;Why are the colonial mages wrecking up my Norse setting?&quot;, why not ask something more along the lines of &quot;In my game I'm planning on having several nameless orders populating the Scandinavian regions cira. XXXX, does anyone have some cool ideas on what they could be?&quot;. One makes people check the books and question how you're getting this from material that doesn't explain things the way you're talking about them, the other would hopefully get some creative juices flowing about things like how Seidr practitioners might be treated, how male mages would be considered Ergi etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1220889#post1220889\">made a point about it in Great Cults topic</a>, moving this subtopic to there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2018, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T23:47:30-07:00","id":1221093,"title":"","content":"Mage goes into the astral and heads to the astral concept to civilization, chats with other mages also at the concept of civilization, done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T01:14:41-07:00","id":1221099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221093#post1221093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage goes into the astral and heads to the astral concept to civilization, chats with other mages also at the concept of civilization, done.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is surprising to me there is very little in the line about Mages doing stuff like this regularly, outside of the Neolithic. Order Temenos Realms mean a whole lot for global cohesion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T01:31:57-07:00","id":1221101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Biston</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221099#post1221099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is surprising to me there is very little in the line about Mages doing stuff like this regularly, outside of the Neolithic. Order Temenos Realms mean a whole lot for global cohesion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the Mysterium merit from the core book is anything to go by, I would propably say that they're the ones most likely to host those kind of sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T01:40:18-07:00","id":1221102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221101#post1221101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If the Mysterium merit from the core book is anything to go by, I would propably say that they're the ones most likely to host those kind of sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've speculated that Egregore might somehow be tied to the Mysterium's Temenos Realm. Especially given it's outright called <i>egregore.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T02:42:47-07:00","id":1221109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221069#post1221069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I only point that each Darshanas Cults have it's own 'native flavor' and may not agree with joining Diamond Orders coalition on just seeing them</b> - and those Cults can just want to stay 'Nameless' longer - just like we see in <i>Princes of Conquered Lands</i> Dark Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a lot of those Darshana/Nameless cults joined the Orders because, by that point, the Orders have <i>resources</i>. They're by definition a group of people from other cultures who have united and share their Artifacts, Grimoires, Masters, Mysteries, cults, and knowledge. What the Dark Eras propose is that many Darshana/Nameless cults 'join' the Orders because accessing those resources is pretty convenient.<br /> <br /> By the way, it's not that those regional cults just sign up in one day and trade all their stuff. It's a cultural assimilation that takes place over generations, just like anything else. Even if the Orders came branding their swords and violently forced cults to join them (which didn't happen!), that doesn't mean the local cults are on board instantly. They would be a lot of resistance, so any assimilation happening would still take place over generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T03:20:57-07:00","id":1221112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221109#post1221109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a lot of those Darshana/Nameless cults joined the Orders because, by that point, the Orders have <i>resources</i>. They're by definition a group of people from other cultures who have united and share their Artifacts, Grimoires, Masters, Mysteries, cults, and knowledge. What the Dark Eras propose is that many Darshana/Nameless cults 'join' the Orders because accessing those resources is pretty convenient.<br /> <br /> By the way, it's not that those regional cults just sign up in one day and trade all their stuff. It's a cultural assimilation that takes place over generations, just like anything else. Even if the Orders came branding their swords and violently forced cults to join them (which didn't happen!), that doesn't mean the local cults are on board instantly. They would be a lot of resistance, so any assimilation happening would still take place over generations.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Reseru</b>, I just find it really odd that 'native' mages before age of mass trade with 'West' would say '<i>I found this weird shaman from across ocean and he said something about Atlantis - now I become Atlantinist and I join their South Orders'</i>. Just imagine Awakened like that in preVikings times on North. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One, maybe two Awakened in native mages community per generation may talk something about Dragons, but that's it. Before mass trade, I do not see concept of large Caucus populations in native Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2018, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T03:49:43-07:00","id":1221115,"title":"","content":"Maybe not Atlantis, but they'd probably speak of a Valhalla that was lost when the last cycle of Ragnar\u00f6k broke reality. They may squabble with Platonic Mages to the south over the details, but both recognize that they speak not of two different events, but of the Fall and the Time Before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T04:11:17-07:00","id":1221118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221112#post1221112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Reseru</b>, I just find it really odd that 'native' mages before age of mass trade with 'West' would say '<i>I found this weird shaman from across ocean and he said something about Atlantis - now I become and I join their South Orders'</i>. Just imagine Awakened like that in preVikings times on North. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One, maybe two Awakened in native mages community per generation may talk something about Dragons, but that's it. Before mass trade, I do not see concept of large Caucus populations in native Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it\u2019s bottom-up and not top-down. Second Chances already said it; instead of starting with the idea that an Atlantean schema must exist as a baseline before mages mingle, start with local cultures and what they have in common. <br /> <br /> After all, that\u2019s how the Darshanas themselves formed amidst the Great Cults.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Well okay, the Diamond <i>does</i> claim the world works in a top-down way. That the seeds of the \u201cAtlantean\u201d Orders always existed all over the world. As Above So Below and all that. But that\u2019s retroactive reasoning and philosophy they came up with <b>after</b> they formed into a coherent society able to last centuries. And since we\u2019re dealing with the phase of their conception, we still have to take historical context into account, and conclude that the Orders formed without a universal philosophy, instead syncretizing gnostic elements from local cultures to create/discover that universal philosophy in the first place.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also worth noting that when the Diamond claim descent from an ideal ur-civilization, most of the time they\u2019re doing for its symbolic weight. Somebody described the Diamond/Atlantean schema as essentially being a communal Shadow Name, and that description fits. When a mage takes Thor as his Shadow Name, he isn\u2019t claiming he\u2019s the literal Norse god. Same with the Diamond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-22-2018, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T07:09:19-07:00","id":1221147,"title":"","content":"Wyrd the point is they didn't do that. It wasn't a instantenous process, cultural assimilation is a slow process that takes a lot of time and happens in real life. And it doesn't have to involve conquest.<br /> <br /> Just took at what happened with Ancient Rome. They conquered ancient greece but in the end they ended up adopting a lot of the culture, mythology and philosophy of the conquered nation. Heracles, son of Zeus became Hercules, son of Jupiter. During the spread of christianity is also assimilated various local myths into its own mythology, X-mass takes place on the day of the winter solitice in the Roman calendar. Old and new beliefs and traditions become synthetized, this has happened thorough history to many times to count. It's a natural process. We're seeing it even now with the advent of globalization, symbols and holidays that have been strictly national have now become more global. Saint Patricks day is celebrated outside Ireland despite it previously being a local thing, same with Halloween. It just happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T07:34:43-07:00","id":1221150,"title":"","content":"&quot;Your Atlantis is my Asgard,<br /> my Ginnungagap your Abyss.<br /> <br /> You like to climb on ladders,<br /> I climb the cosmic tree.<br /> <br /> The way you look and talk,<br /> won't make me lose a beat.<br /> <br /> Because all that matters<br /> is that we trade cool shit&quot;<br /> <br /> *Awakened Skald out*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T11:33:06-07:00","id":1221217,"title":"","content":"Limited Edition Lightsabers, just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T11:43:18-07:00","id":1221220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221217#post1221217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limited Edition Lightsabers, just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am very confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T11:53:26-07:00","id":1221224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221220#post1221220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am very confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>First page of this conversation, I summarize how the Diamond Orders and Exarch Cults (and later, the Free Council) don't grab people and how they instead do grab people in my usual sardonic way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T12:12:26-07:00","id":1221231,"title":"","content":"One thing that relates to all of this is how the Norse (along with a lot of people in Europa around the time discussed) handled the sort of ideas we're talking about. Namely, they just kind of added it in, and over time these things took root.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Atlantean Dogma&quot; is nowhere near as insistent as the Christian Dogma, for example, but as a point of comparison, a lot of the Norse just did not give a shit about adding Jesus and Elohim to their pantheon, accepting it as a substrata of what they believed. Over time, as the grindstone was steadily applied, Christianity became more and more of a thing, and most people just didn't give a shit about whether or not who they were getting their blessings from, so long as they got them and could blame/attribute things to their name. Really, if Christianity had been more invasive than it was, it probably would have been rejected.<br /> <br /> The model of the Diamond Orders is less insistent than that, since pretty much every mage since the era of To The Strongest has realized that it is a description of reality that's about as actually real as any of the Great Cults that started the entire shindig off in it's actuality-but the <i>shape</i> of it fits better and even fills the holes they own worldviews leave empty. That said, regional versions do exist. At any point in the slide from the Aesir worship to the full Christianity worship, Mages would probably be disillusioned by their own world religion (because the nature of Awakening means that even the most devout people in the age are going to recognize the Lie inherent in worship), however it's mixed, and probably describe the Atlantean model in whatever the socio-religious-occult context of the time was because that's what's easiest to talk about.<br /> <br /> THis might be one of the most important things to realize, actually-upon Awakening, religions lose their reverence. Religions become, not a way to worship, but a way to <i>describe-</i>and as anyone who has had someone pick apart any metaphor they use know, descriptions have limits. Very early mage cults and cabals might lean heavily on their religion, but that's because alternative models do not yet exist. THey don't even need to be subjected to other modes of thoughts to realize things fall apart, but when they are confronted with people whose own understanding fill out the puzzle that much better, mages (being drawn to truth) are more likely accept what describes a thing <i>truly</i> over their own cultural upbringing than not.<br /> <br /> The Atlantean model of the Diamond works because, while it has the trappings of a religion, it is really more just of an empirical observation of reality with an easy to digest narrative layer on top of it-and that narrative layer can flex and flux to work with people because the story it portrays is not as important as the wholeness of reality that it describes.<br /> <br /> Or, put another way, the &quot;Atlantean dogma&quot; works as well as it does <i>because</i> everyone knows it's only a model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-22-2018, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T12:26:14-07:00","id":1221235,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna chip in with my own headcanon.<br /> <br /> The existence and general shape of the orders are enforced with some imperial spells. It is not so much mind control as mages simply tend to organize themselves that way because that is how reality is &quot;supposed&quot; to look. Kill of all members of the orders and in<br /> a decade mages would organize themselves in similar patters,<br /> 2 decades realize that they have a lot in common with mages 2 towns over who also happen to value martial might<br /> 3 decades a loosely connected web of mages calling themselves the adamantine sword spans the world with significant amounts of local variations of course.<br /> <br /> A similar sequence would play out for the other orders<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T05:34:14-07:00","id":1221455,"title":"","content":"In my usual attempt of getting lurking instincts and social anxiety out my system, I looked away from my comfy little corner of world and, through what I can only describe as the opposite of looking for a needle in a haystack, had a sort of moment of clarity about these threads.<br /> <br /> I'm late, I know. But I always miss out about what's going on around me and I learned the hard way that I need to chill, read and meditate before expressing rushed opinions.<br /> <br /> *takes a deep breath*<br /> <br /> Since Kieron Gillen taught me that I should try to be nicer:<br /> <br /> Ok Wyrd, I don't know if this is pointless or not, but let's try to tackle the issue in another way, just for the sake of trying to solve the questions this topic asks. <br /> <br /> It's clear that the idea of the supernatural societies of the various places being strongly tied with the &quot;flavor&quot; of the local human culture is something that enjoy a lot, to the point where you like to ramp it up more than the standard CoD usually does. Direct connection to clear-cut ideas of what impact myths and traditions should have on the setting. Sometimes things get more stylized than usual in the process, but you'd rather have a strong structure with blunt answers where the elements you want to use are clearly defined and kept apart from others, if simplified a bit. Modern Scandinavian Wolves have a Shadow, traditions and enemies to deal with that all owe to Norse mythology in a rather literal way and, Viking Mages never mention Atlantis or the Diamond and so on.<br /> <br /> It's fine. Not how I roll, in the CoD I like my connections to human religions to be murky, vague and more of a guideline, <i>at best</i>, but it's fine. I don't think you're alone on that.<br /> <br /> What I want to ask so that we can discuss it and see if we get to a place that solves your doubts is: what really says that your perspective loses legitimacy if foreign cultures come into contact? Let's put aside the how and when for a second, even though that's a question this thread already answered. I'm asking you if human cultures shape your setting so much, should not they be able to endure contact with others with ease? What breaks if a Viking Mage meets a Greek one? Who says they should stab each other the moment they notice their cultural background differs? Can we get over the fact that there's no Atlantean Nation, Euro-Roman or not, waging a cultural war against the world? <b>Does it really matter to your game?</b> And I say &quot;your game&quot;, because let's be real: that's what these threads are actually about, neutral title or not.<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna tackle other issues or criticism the whole meta-discussion brings up because...no, I just won't. Having said that, I'm trying to at least provide a contribution to the topic at hand.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T09:58:19-07:00","id":1221491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221455#post1221455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want to ask so that we can discuss it and see if we get to a place that solves your doubts is: what really says that your perspective loses legitimacy if foreign cultures come into contact? Let's put aside the how and when for a second, even though that's a question this thread already answered. I'm asking you if human cultures shape your setting so much, should not they be able to endure contact with others with ease? What breaks if a Viking Mage meets a Greek one? Who says they should stab each other the moment they notice their cultural background differs? Can we get over the fact that there's no Atlantean Nation, Euro-Roman or not, waging a cultural war against the world? <b>Does it really matter to your game?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>does</i> matter - simply on logical reasoning on this setting. Let's look on example - <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> Dark Era points start of Viking Age as circa 800 AD. So any contacts with Roman-civilized Awakened before this year will be contacts of preViking Norse. Now, if we have preVikings Norse mages meeting Roman Awakened that journeyed on North, long before Sleepers, he brings with him his knowledge. Like, for example, Latin and Greek. As Norse Awakened have access to the same Arcana as Roman one - they can easily copy his knowledge of Latin and Greek with simple Mind spells. And this knowledge spread in the preViking Norse mages culture. More, Norse mages can teach those mundane skills to Norse Sleepers. As we started in preVikings time - let's say 100 years before - we easily can have whole Norse villages or armies fluent in Latin. And then we have things like better Latin speaking Norse berserkers than christian monk they did not seen ( or any book ) in their life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T11:07:18-07:00","id":1221507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221491#post1221491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Norse Awakened have access to the same Arcana as Roman one - they can easily copy his knowledge of Latin and Greek with simple Mind spells. And this knowledge spread in the preViking Norse mages culture. More, Norse mages can teach those mundane skills to Norse Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes multiple things that are not self-evident:<br /> <br /> 1. That foreign mages will default to spells for personal communication when they can all perceive High Speech without extra investment in specific branches of magic.<br /> 2. That Universal Language (and Mind 3) is commonplace and widely used.<br /> 3. That mage characters will freely share knowledge with their Sleeper communities in ways that do not factor into their own goals and inclination to secrecy.<br /> 4. That learning a foreign language that is only used by mystics and their acolytes is going to be a priority for the average Sleeper to the level of widespread use long before contact with that language's native mundane bearers.<br /> <br /> It's not the Neolithic anymore, man, the Awakened aren't openly known to hold influence over the world and accorded a place of respect within it as a matter of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T12:34:04-07:00","id":1221525,"title":"","content":"Latin is only one example. With Roman-civilized Awakened showing up on the North, I can have any common discovery that Roman and related cultures have to show up centuries before Norse culture get historically contact on them in Viking Age. Basically, open travel of Diamond Orders mages around the world breaks any historical timeline of Sleeper society events. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Literally you can tell 'mages did it'. Any historical games feel is thrown out of window.<br /> <br /> <b>I much more would see whole clue of this topic as 'world travel of Diamond Orders is possible, but until Sleepers mass trade with particular culture - it's limited to only few small events'.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-23-2018, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T12:52:58-07:00","id":1221527,"title":"","content":"So, by that logic, every human on the planet is fluent in English based on the fact English speakers appear all over the world and mass media has a focus on English. Glad to know exposure to a single language has led to its universal adoption and use. I mean, snark aside, that\u2019s a terrible example and I really don\u2019t see why there are a couple dozen threads now exploring your personal bugbear with Mage as presented in a setting. Especially when things such as the Tremere existing in Norse lands is part of the setting, and they originated in Ancient Egypt, something even older than To the Strongest, so the setting as a whole supports Mages exploring, being part of human diasporas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T13:32:56-07:00","id":1221534,"title":"","content":"See, that's the core of the problem. Just because Mages have the means and inclination to explore, it does not mean they hold globalization raves in the Temenos where thousands of Awakened discuss how to impose One Single Culture over the whole planet.<br /> <br /> There's a leap in logic between &quot;Mages do travel and are more inclined to syncretize new beliefs and discoveries in their arsenal of observational tools than destroying it&quot; and &quot;Everything is everywhere anytime and nothing means nothing&quot; that I just can't fathom. And people have told you why that's not the case multiple times.<br /> <br /> You have issues with parts of the setting. You ask why those perceived issues exist, understandably so, and people tell why that's the case, providing motivations. Again and again. If you keep going to square 1 expecting that someday the gamelines will throw what they've established away to support your thing, it's not gonna happen. And I gotta be honest and say that the fact other's people's opinion, which you keep asking for, looks nothing more than white noise to you , it's more than a bit disheartening. Because when even the books' writers come down from the Supernal and offer you their take, only for you to ignore it and ask again some time later as if nothing happened, I don't think you'll ever find a satisfactory answer.<br /> <br /> All while keeping in mind that if you don't like something in the books, you change it for your personal canon, but it's also true that you cannot expect the books to agree with you once you move in that territory.<br /> <br /> Annoyed emoticons or not (like, really?).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T13:48:24-07:00","id":1221536,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/spongefan/images/2/23/Tulio_head_banging.gif/revision/latest?cb=20150612222916\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I once expressed this before, Hamster, and I will say it again:<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>IF YOU ARE GOING TO IGNORE WHAT PEOPLE TELL YOU, KINDLY STOP WASTING OUR TIME BY ASKING IN THE FIRST PLACE.</i></u></b><br /> <br /> You have an era where there is going to be cultural exchange, you've had the difference between Roman Christian expansionism and Atlantean syncretism explained thousands of times and how they are different and how to use/approach them, and you have been given ideas on how to do your own take on what you want(which is basically the Diamond filling in for Christianity if Christianity only ever expanded via crusade and the Nameless Orders of various cultures being Ascension-like groups), <i>and you are still not listening because you want the game to reflect what you faultily believe, <u>and you are never going to get that</u></i>.<br /> <br /> Either change the game you're playing here on the forums, or kindly just <i>stop</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T13:57:08-07:00","id":1221537,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I'm honestly not sure what you get out of doing this to yourself over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T15:00:34-07:00","id":1221552,"title":"","content":"For me it just looks like mistaking one's own headcanon for actual canon and then complaining that it doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> Also this topic starts devolving into &quot;everyone vs wyrdhamster&quot; so I think it's better to just leave since the same arguments get repeated and there is no progres in the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T21:43:46-07:00","id":1221615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221527#post1221527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when things such as the Tremere existing in Norse lands is part of the setting, and they originated in Ancient Egypt, something even older than To the Strongest, so the setting as a whole supports Mages exploring, being part of human diasporas.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\"><b>Tremere Legacy <i>are not</i> stated to be in the North in preViking Era - the Seo Hel are</b></a> - which were <i>different </i>Legacy that Tremere devoured them in High Middle Ages and changed later into Tremere House. ( Same was with Nagaraja Legacy in <i>To the Strongest</i>. ) Different Legacies that are only connected by idea of them being Reapers. In 8th century Tremere merely show themselves up in the East of Europe, they were long before showing on North without Diamond Orders support of them. I suspect Tremere plague on North would start in circa 800, when first Vikings return from first contacts with Europeans on continent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-24-2018, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T23:09:54-07:00","id":1221619,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but where are you getting that from, I just reread Seo Hel to make sure and all it says is that they were in the region, but then the Tremere came and ate them (and got some wicked heart burn). I mean honestly, where are you getting the idea that the Norse were extreme isolationists and didn't have contact with anyone in the surrounding regions? Historically they were quite mobile folks, trading up and down the European waterways and coastlines, not to mention venturing much further afield (such as Canadian shores). To the Strongest happens about one thousand and one hundred years before anything resembling what we currently think of as Norse or Viking peoples. That's a hell of a lot of time for ideas to percolate, especially among people who are meant to be driven by their thirst for mysteries and obsessions. In over a thousand years, no one said &quot;Hey buddy, what'cha think is over that hill? I hear there are some people that worship a giant magic tree, you think it could be that celestial ladder thing? Let's go ask eh?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T00:16:47-07:00","id":1221624,"title":"","content":"Yeah...at the most basic level, the Diamond Orders just claimed ownership of archetypes. When they met new groups of mages, they approached the closest ones who fit said archetype or the philosophy and say &quot;We are reflections of the same Supernal truth. We'll let you play with our stuff if you share our ideas. Friends?&quot;<br /> Only then does the assimulation begin.<br /> <br /> Orders are not 'merely' organizations. They are Archetypes.<br /> <br /> Combined with the greater ease of travel and communication they have over historically accurate mundanes; who did have contact with the groups in question, it is not a hard sell to say the Orders were there.<br /> <br /> A better question is &quot;What did they look like in the local area?&quot; Heck for most of history, &quot;Who are the prelate/Seers?&quot; works.<br /> <br /> The Exarch Cults have clearly existed during these periods but unlike the Diamond Orders, they don't naturally revolve around an archetype or an ideal. Given what we know, it seems likely existed within the Diamond Orders before being cast out (and declared Nameless). Which would make assimulating local structures more difficult. (&quot;Yeah, your priest friend can't play with us, because his deity is an evil tyrant whose actions disrupt our research.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T04:26:31-07:00","id":1221649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221624#post1221624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orders are not 'merely' organizations. They are Archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention, the Orders not just appropriated and came to embody universal Archetypes that exist in any human society/culture, over time they have developed a strong representation in the Supernal thanks to the actions of sympathetic Archmages (esp. the Exemplar faction, but not necessarily just them), Ascended mages (ditto; heck, we know the life work of one Ascended was enough to reshape the nature of magic and one Order), the Oracles (if they indeed exist), and the Exarchs (for the Seers). Moreover, if the Free Order is correct, the very global success of the Orders was probably going to give them a meaningful imprint in the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Due to the way the Supernal works, this pattern originally developed from ground up at certain points in the timeline, but now spreads its influence forward and backward across all of history and the world, although apparently not Neolithic prehistory, perhaps because of the temporal proximity of the Time Before acting as a screen. This now makes the Orders destined to happen; as others remarked, even if the Orders were somehow wiped out, new generations of mages in all likelihood would inevitably organize themselves spontaneously to recreate them. This is not going to change, unless the Supernal gets rewritten to give Awakened society a different 'natural' pattern, and mankind a different set of Archetypes.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, the Orders have grown into quite powerful Shadow Names that mages can adopt and embody to draw power from, the more they do so, the stronger the symbols become and the more power they can provide to their followers, and the more mages all over the world get naturally drawn to use them. It is a virtuous cycle with near-infinite potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T05:29:06-07:00","id":1221664,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand, Orders as organizations would not exist in pre-Viking Scandinavia. You would have either a lot of solitary mages sometimes exchanging knowledge, or loose organisations of like-minded mages. Some of them would be pretty similar to existing Diamond Orders or Seers - secretive scholars, power-hungry tyrants, war mages, etc. But culturally they would be Norse, using Nordic religious trappings, etc.<br /> <br /> What happens when Diamond mages contact Norse ones? Some cultural exchange is going to take place even if antagonistic (robbing foreign mages of their secrets and Artefacts). In the long run, the Orders will probably win. They have more mages, which mean more secrets, more Rotes, more Artifacts that could potentially interest Norse mages. Culturally they are much easier to adopt - you can believe in Odin and still accept the basic tenets of Adamantine Arrow, while a Christian follower would have problems with accepting explanations of a local cult which constantly references the Allfather.<br /> <br /> In the long run, the local associations won't survive. Unless they have some unique knowledge the Diamond doesn't, they have less to offer to their prospective members. They are either going to be absorbed by 'Atlanteans', losing a lot of their distinctiveness, or isolate themselves and become Nameless Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13425-gantolandon","name":"Gantolandon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T05:49:51-07:00","id":1221668,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, you seem to think that cultures form in a stasis, a closed system. They do not. &quot;viking&quot; culture is a misnomer, there is no viking culture, they where as you all probably know only a small fraction of people in the larger ethno-cultural group known as Norse. So first things first, their culture didn't just pop-up around 800 common era, it was built on previous cultures in Scandinavia and Germania. These cultures all had influence, relations and contacts with nearby cultures in Europe. The Roman empire had cultural influence over the pre-viking cultures and European cultures after the fall of West Rome had influence over Scandinavian cultures. That's because cultures share ideas and trade with each other and when ideas are changed between parties, ideas take hold, mix and match with ones own culture and make something new or just borrow it head on. There where &quot;vikings&quot; before some Norsemen decided to attack a British monastery, and most of &quot;viking culture&quot; existed far longer then the end of the Viking era. Because culture is complicated and seldom, if ever, completely erased and 'painted over'. <br /> But cultural exchange between the Roman Empire in ~800 common era (e.g. the Byzantines) and Scandinavians where probably very limited. <br /> <br /> Now speaking of the Mage setting here, as other has pointed out, there is no Romano-Greek cultural war/invasion going on around the globe, but cultural exchange and isomorphic melting of ideas. Viking mages are sure to have something akin to local orders, archetypal to what the diamond have, similar but distinct. Some form of Politicians/spies/warriors/lore-keepers and a philosophy based in old Norse pagan tradition that can help explain their view of the supernal. When these meet with Greek/Roman mages they exchange world-view and philosophies and both their ideas might evolve. For instance, the Byzantine tradition probably talks about the Greco-Roman Gods being evil bastards that now control the world and with it the myths of Jupiter/Zeus and his brothers taking over the world from the Titans. Atlantean myth would probably not be the cultural hegemonic idea in Europe until they get more cultural exchange with the Arabs and get back much of the lost Greek writings and Platos' ideas comes back to take hold culturally later on in the middle ages. The vikings might as suggested earlier have a picture about the fall that involves an earlier Ragnar\u00f6k, or perhaps that Oden, Vile and Ve killed the old giant Ymer and reconstructed the world with his body, and and constructed the rainbow bridge for mages to be allowed into the magical realm of Asg\u00e5rd and learn magic from the All-Father, perhaps the Norse see their trickster gods as similar to what the Greco-Romans would call an amalgamation between the Oracles/Watchtowers/Exarchs. <br /> <br /> The point is, culture don't destroy one another, they mix and intertwine, the mingle and exchange ideas. But cultural ideas as seldom just thrown away just because the're as &quot;better&quot; alternative. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T06:25:18-07:00","id":1221684,"title":"","content":"A tangentially related side-thought: A game starring archmages may be where all this culture wars and invasions take place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:03:23-07:00","id":1221689,"title":"","content":"I do get that Diamond Orders exchange with local 'Nameless' Orders/ Darshanas cults, 'Atlanteans' do not threaten with the help of spells (usually). <b>The question is WHEN Diamond made contact with local mages in each instance, starting the exchange. </b>Because from some of you telling - Diamond Orders, Greco-Roman mages just visit every corner of the world in generation, two after creation of Orders ( i.e. circa 200 BCE ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So by this it would mean you cannot have untouched by 'Atlanteans' local cults from 150 BCE onward, as Diamond were literally <i>everywhere</i> on the globe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( That's interpretations is also contradicting official material like<i> Princes of Conquered Lands </i>Dark Era pointing that most of Mutapa Empire is still under Mutupos, Four Totems model of cults, not proper part of Diamond Orders in 1600 years later. )<br /> <br /> In our Vikings Era example, starting date of <i>Wolf &amp; Raven </i>Dark Era is circa 700 AD. 700 AD is 900 years later than creation of Diamond Orders, only 2500 kilometers from Rome. If your theories will be right, then in Norse you will have full Diamond conversion by this time, nothing more than few 'old school' Nameless following Old Magic of area. All original Norse Darshana cults will be subsumed into Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( With weird, Greco-Roman organisations and titles before even Vikings raids. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:17:30-07:00","id":1221696,"title":"","content":"Well first contact between Roman mages and Scandinavian mages probably happened in Roman times, at least 5th century, probably a few centuries earlier. But no, it takes more then just simple contact to erradicate local customs, traditions and cultures. The're probably smaller things that influenced them form that time. But Scandinavia wasn't Christianized for over a 1000 years (on paper) after the death of Jesus.<br /> But for things, where does it say that the Diamond emerged in Rome? I can't seem to find this information.<br /> And to be fair, muslim lands is probably the stronghold for the diamond in this era.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All original Norse Darshana cults will be subsumed into Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( With weird, Greco-Roman organisations and titles before even Vikings raids. ) </div> </div> </div>I have literally no clue as of how you came to this conclusion.,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:40:11-07:00","id":1221702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221696#post1221696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first contact between Roman mages and Scandinavian mages probably happened in Roman times, at least 5th century, probably a few centuries earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if we have 'few centuries earlier' we come to numbers of like 2nd century AD - implying that Diamond, with their whole Greco-Roman trappings will be on rise in 8th century Vikings Era - it's 5 centuries times we talk here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221696#post1221696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But no, it takes more then just simple contact to erradicate local customs, traditions and cultures. The're probably smaller things that influenced them form that time. But Scandinavia wasn't Christianized for over a 1000 years (on paper) after the death of Jesus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time and time again in this very topic I was pointed that I should not look over Christianization of culture ( or Islamization? ) for indication of Diamond Orders main influence in the area. I would agree that Diamond conversion should end with full Christianization of North - but other forumers told many times it's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221696#post1221696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for things, where does it say that the Diamond emerged in Rome? I can't seem to find this information.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's implied few times in 1E and 2E books - full analysis is in topic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakened</a>. See parts from 200 BCE. There is even quote in Adamantine Arrow Order Origin write-up in 2E corebook.<br /> <br /> <i>'The Adamantine Arrow is both the oldest and youngest Order. Like most of the Diamond Orders, the Arrow\u2019s core formed in the Hellenistic era, circa 200 BCE, primarily from an Indian school of magical philosophy called the Vajrastra (\u201cThunderbolt Weapons\u201d). '</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221696#post1221696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to be fair, Muslim lands is probably the stronghold for the diamond in this era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More to it, as Arabic lands are ex-Roman Empire provinces, I would say that Diamond was there in 100 BCE, 1st century AD, at most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221696#post1221696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have literally no clue as of how you came to this conclusion.,</div> </div> </div> </div>All my Mage books point that Diamond Orders use Latin and Greek based titles and Roman-based law system in Consilia - that is also Latin based term. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:01:20-07:00","id":1221711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221702#post1221702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More to it, as Arabic lands are ex-Roman Empire provinces, I would say that Diamond was there in 100 BCE, 1st century AD, at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>That statement is massively misleading (says the historian who studied Roman and Islamic history).<br /> <br /> Are the Levant, Maghrib, and Anatolia former Roman provinces? Yes. Was there an inheritance of Roman knowledge? Yes. Is Arabia? Khorasan? Transoxiana? Sub-Saharan Africa? India? These are all Islamic lands in which Arabs ruled. None of them is an ex-Roman province. The Islamic tradition is derived from Greco-Roman knowledge, but it also draws heavily on Indian and Chinese discoveries. I agree that the Islamic Golden Age would also be a Golden Age for Mages, but that is because it is a synthesis of culture, science, and tradition from across Afro-Eurasia, not just because they are the inheritors of Rome (that role falls to the Eastern Roman Empire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:18:35-07:00","id":1221713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221702#post1221702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if we have 'few centuries earlier' we come to numbers of like 2nd century AD - implying that Diamond, with their whole Greco-Roman trappings will be on rise in 8th century Vikings Era - it's 5 centuries times we talk here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That year would be fair to assume to be about the time for first contact between the two groups. No it's not sure that those &quot;trappings will be on the rise&quot;. Culture just ain't copied like that. Mages don't just copy the predominated view of another mage culture, it's a process that need time, distance and interaction etc. Norse mages are necessarily no more Roman then their sleeper counterpart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time and time again in this very topic I was pointed that I should not look over Christianization of culture ( or Islamization? ) for indication of Diamond Orders main influence in the area. I would agree that Diamond conversion should end with full Christianization of North - but other forumers told many times it's not. </div> </div> </div>It was just a comparison that change can take time, not that these separate things need to coincidence with one another. And to be precise, Christianity on paper ain't the same thing as non-paganism among the populace. We still have pre-christian, pagan traditions although we'd been &quot;christians&quot; for almost a millennium. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's implied few times in 1E and 2E books - full analysis is in topic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakened</a>. See parts from 200 BCE. There is even quote in Adamantine Arrow Order Origin write-up in 2E corebook.<br /> <br /> <i>'The Adamantine Arrow is both the oldest and youngest Order. Like most of the Diamond Orders, the Arrow\u2019s core formed in the Hellenistic era, circa 200 BCE, primarily from an Indian school of magical philosophy called the Vajrastra (\u201cThunderbolt Weapons\u201d). '</i> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know it's implied at places. But as far as I know, nowhere does it point to Rome, or even the Roman Republic. The Hellenistic World is huge and cover large sways of land that never was touched by Roman borders. In 200 BCE the Roman Republic was not much larger the modern Italy. It's unlikely that the Diamond was formed in Rome, and the foundations of the Orders are definitely not roman. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\"> Of course. ;) More to it, as Arabic lands are ex-Roman Empire provinces, I would say that Diamond was there in 100 BCE, 1st century AD, at most.</pre> </div>Yes, but they are also Persian and Hindu lands, African and philistine lands... I'd say it's more likely it was formed somewhere in mesopotamia or around there, modern day Iran,Iraq, Pakistan and or around, far more likely in Persia or some Greek state then in Rome. (Unless there's a word of God that says it's in Rome, but that would just be eurocentric :P ) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All my Mage books point that Diamond Orders use Latin and Greek based titles and Roman-based law system in Consilia - that is also Latin based term. </div> </div> </div>I was talking about the local orders/cults being subsumed into the diamond already in ~7-9th century. The titles are still today local and it has probably more with the spread of Romanesque culture then mages themselves. Norse (arab/frankish/iranian/axum/even roman and greek) ) mages are far more likely to use local tradition, customs and titles then any form of Concilia we would recognize today. This is like saying that everything in the Mage setting should have English names because everything is named in English. Most names are derivatives from Greek/latin/indian and a few other languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:58:56-07:00","id":1221723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221713#post1221713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages don't just copy the predominated view of another mage culture, it's a process that need time, distance and interaction etc. Norse mages are necessarily no more Roman then their sleeper counterpart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Norse mages are just much more Roman than their sleeper counterpart simply because mages meet other mages. Where going to the South for Sleepers is years long journey - so only some war bands may meet Roman culture - Awakened, just as pointed in this very topic, can teleport on the other end of continent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221713#post1221713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was just a comparison that change can take time, not that these separate things need to coincidence with one another. And to be precise, Christianity on paper ain't the same thing as non-paganism among the populace. We still have pre-christian, pagan traditions although we'd been &quot;christians&quot; for almost a millennium.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is difference between 'We, Norse mages, have our own local cults and magical traditions' and 'We all are in Diamond now, I just use Odin in magic style cause I like him'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221713#post1221713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about the local orders/cults being subsumed into the diamond already in ~7-9th century. The titles are still today local and it has probably more with the spread of Romanesque culture then mages themselves. Norse (arab/frankish/iranian/axum/even roman and greek) ) mages are far more likely to use local tradition, customs and titles then any form of Concilia we would recognize today. This is like saying that everything in the Mage setting should have English names because everything is named in English. Most names are derivatives from Greek/latin/indian and a few other languages.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is... fairly good point. Still, if Diamond use trappings of local culture - and those Darshanas Cults are similar to the Archetypes Orders use - what's the difference between Diamond Orders and Darshanas Cults in the first place? Beside talking about Atlantis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:59:29-07:00","id":1221724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221713#post1221713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 200 BCE the Roman Republic was not much larger the modern Italy. It's unlikely that the Diamond was formed in Rome, and the foundations of the Orders are definitely not roman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Year 200 BCE is literally 1 year after Second <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punic_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Punic War</a> between Rome and Carthage, where Rome takes one third of Middeterenian Sea, starting centuries long conquest of Europe. It's the literal start of Roman power in Europe and greatest Empire on the continent in that time. In year 200 BCE map looks like this:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://110101-313254-raikfcquaxqncofqfm.stackpathdns.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/europe200bc2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Only 150 years later, Rome conquared half of Europe and Minor Asia. In 30 BCE maps look like this:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://110101-313254-raikfcquaxqncofqfm.stackpathdns.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/europe30bc.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221713#post1221713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but they are also Persian and Hindu lands, African and philistine lands... I'd say it's more likely it was formed somewhere in mesopotamia or around there, modern day Iran,Iraq, Pakistan and or around, far more likely in Persia or some Greek state then in Rome. (Unless there's a word of God that says it's in Rome, but that would just be eurocentric :P )</div> </div> </div> </div><i>To the Strongest</i> Dark Era points that in Greece, Persia and India you have various Darshanas Cults that are more and more interlinked, each year from year 300 BCE. To this day I do not remember single pointing of creation of Orders in books, but Diamond quickly can convert Darshanas Cults in those lands as those are <i>already</i> Hellenistic, from Alexander's Empire. And pointing that Orders were created in Greece is also eurocentric. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-24-2018, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:08:28-07:00","id":1221726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221723#post1221723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakened, just as pointed in this very topic, can teleport on the other end of continent.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way sympathy works means this is not remotely as simple as it sounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:10:53-07:00","id":1221747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221723#post1221723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Norse mages are just much more Roman than their sleeper counterpart simply because mages meet other mages. Where going to the South for Sleepers is years long journey - so only some war bands may meet Roman culture - Awakened, just as pointed in this very topic, can teleport on the other end of continent.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make this easier then it is. And even so, there would be a thousand (probably way more) sleepers that made these journeys then there are mages. People, simple meet other people.<br /> You're making your whole argument by saying that I would be Chinese just because I've met a few of them and they are a way larger culture then mine and I'd studied mandarin for a few months.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is... fairly good point. Still, if Diamond use trappings of local culture - and those Darshanas Cults are similar to the Archetypes Orders use - what's the difference between Diamond Orders and Darshanas Cults in the first place? Beside talking about Atlantis? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that Darshana cults are a thing outside the context of the Strongest era. I do believe context and coherence around a common culture, eg. Diamond/atlantean dogma would be the largest difference beside scale. There is a point to be made that the Great Cults and Darshanas will converge and evolve into the Diamond, with more outside influence over time and some things winning over other and other things lost from the Diamond. Part of these cults and Darshanas might be around today in their own right, but in different form even.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Year 200 BCE is literally 1 year after Second <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punic_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Punic War</a> between Rome and Carthage, where Rome takes half of Middeteranin Sea, starting centuries long conquest of Europe.<br /> It's the literal start of Roman power in Europe and greatest Empire on the continent in that time </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I'm aware. The coast of Spain is also part of it, so slightly larger then modern Italy is still a thing, even if it's a slight understatment. However it's a far less faulty one then &quot;half the<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"> Mediterranean&quot;. I'm still not following how the the birth of the Diamond Orders around 200 would be in Rome just because Rome <i>will</i> be a great superpower in Europe, when almost all their (the orders) cultural influence comes from a melting pot about 2000-3000 km away. Rome might be a cool and great empire in it's own might, but not much speaks for that to be the cradle of the Diamond Orders. Surely they where in Rome, they grew and evolved there but their culture and their mythology and their philosophy comes from the east.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 05-24-2018, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:22:35-07:00","id":1221750,"title":"","content":"In relation to main subtopic about Vikings mages - this how looks map of Europe in year 750 AD.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://110101-313254-raikfcquaxqncofqfm.stackpathdns.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/europead750.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:03:50-07:00","id":1221787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221689#post1221689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diamond Orders, Greco-Roman mages</div> </div> </div> </div><b><u><i>STOP. CALLING. THEM. GRECO-ROMAN.</i></u></b><br /> <br /> The Diamond emerged from a fucking fusion of Greek, Persian, Egyptian, and Indian cultures. You would be more accurate calling them Middle Eastern mages, and you would still be wrong.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>STOP. CALLING. THEM. GRECO-ROMAN.</i></u></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T01:32:29-07:00","id":1221964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221787#post1221787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u><i>STOP. CALLING. THEM. GRECO-ROMAN.</i></u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking here in context of Norse mages meeting European Diamond mages - that would be raised in Greco-Roman culture of Medieval Christanity. Stop being needlessly unpleasant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-25-2018, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T03:01:01-07:00","id":1221975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221702#post1221702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All my Mage books point that Diamond Orders use Latin and Greek based titles and Roman-based law system in Consilia - that is also Latin based term. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to point out that the Order books are written from a twenty-first century standpoint. Just because the Mages of today use a bunch of Greco-Roman terminology doesn\u2019t mean that they used those exact same terms during the Roman era, or made everyone else use \u2018em. Western Civilization post-Renaissance has just had a huge crush on that time period, which was likely (and here I am making assumptions) reflected in the formal codifications of the Diamond Orders post-Renaissance.<br /> <br /> Just because the Arrow draws its roots back to the Hellenistic wonderworkers of Alexander\u2019s court does not mean that the Diamond Orders of today are an unbroken chain of two-thousand-year-old dogma.<br /> <br /> Rather, the 21st-century Arrow owes his heritage to the many willworkers who have come before: the legionnaires and athletes of Rome who honed themselves in a culture falling apart; the hunters and warriors of India who sought to bring the external world and the internal world into harmony; and, yes, the men of the north who knew that the gods themselves were doomed to die and that the worth of a man lay in what he did and how he served his community.<br /> <br /> These various traditions swirl and mix, and we who work magic today do so in their shadows, and we claim all of them under the banner of the Arrow (but one they would not have recognized; an arrow is but a symbol, one of many).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T04:20:22-07:00","id":1221984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221964#post1221964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking here in context of Norse mages meeting European Diamond mages - that would be raised in Greco-Roman culture of Medieval Christanity. Stop being needlessly unpleasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unpleasant perhaps, but needless not. Saying the European mages are just \u201cGreco-Roman\u201d is like saying Americans are English. <br /> <br /> And to nitpick just a bit more: While the Diamond uses Roman/Greek titles, a lot of their actual concepts and tenets behind them are from Hindu and/or Buddhist beliefs. (And guess which culture uses the word \u2018diamond\u2019 as a metaphor for divine perfection). If we start assigning a clear-cut cultural association with the Diamond because of portions of its society/culture/beliefs, I\u2019d go for the Proto-Indo-Europeans. Which I shouldn\u2019t, since then I\u2019d be ignoring all the Greek, Persian, Kemetic etc influences within. <br /> <br /> Just take it easy, man. Mapping perfect, one-to-one correspondences between present/past real life groups and the various supernaturals\u2019 factions in the CofD is trying to weave gold out of straw. I\u2019d dare not try it until I get my hands on a magic lamp or something and thus save myself some frustration, and I highly recommend you do too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-25-2018, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T11:21:01-07:00","id":1222090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world?p=1221964#post1221964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking here in context of Norse mages meeting European Diamond mages - that would be raised in Greco-Roman culture of Medieval Christanity. Stop being needlessly unpleasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, if you are talking about Diamond mages literally from the Greco-Roman region of the world, you have got to say that more clearly. The way you have been doing it this entire time, it has sounded like you were conflating the two, with you even at one point deliberately saying the Diamond was basically a Greco-Roman affair with some Hindu touches without explaining that the reason it's like this is because you are thinking about the fact that these mages in your conflict are Greco-Roman and therefore biased towards that interpretation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Pro-tip, if you are talking about areas, call them Greek or Roman, not Greco-Roman. Given the context you are looking at, you mean Roman. You want to call them Roman Diamond mages rather than Greco-Roman Diamond mages because Greco-Roman in this context describes a cultural foundation rather than a political/regional one.<br /> <br /> This mishap also still does not excuse the fact that mages are often...not divorced, but at an odd angle from their home societies. You gotta remember, the very nature of Awakening casts all societal norms into question, and while it is still human nature to cling to the familiar, mages are still likely to be among the more taboo of their culture. All of this is before you account for how the Diamond operates, the fact that Diamond philosophy at the time heavily diverges from Roman Christian thought, and a wide number of other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-25-2018, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T15:41:11-07:00","id":1222117,"title":"","content":"Considering the known influences of the Diamond Orders, it makes more sense for the Latin influences you keep pointing out to have actually been acquired AFTER the fall of the Roman Empire. <br /> <br /> Think about it; the Diamond Orders organize themselves around the communal 'shadow name' of Atlantis. That is to say, they use &quot;fallen empire&quot; as a unifying resonating symbol, and even more specifically &quot;idealized past&quot;. I can easily imagine 8th century European Mages looking back at the ruins of Rome, reading the ancient texts of that fallen empire, and saying &quot;As High Speech is to Atlantis and Atlantis is to Us, so Latin is to Rome, and Rome is to the Sleepers&quot;, and then adopting Latin because of this symbolism. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, actual Roman-era mages are more likely to use other, more apt metaphors of their times. For example, between the 1st and 4th centuries, various 'mystery cults' with purported Eastern roots were popular; Mithras (Persian origin), Cybele (Anatolian origin), and Isis (Egyptian origin) are only the most famous examples, each with links to previous fallen empires. These would strengthen the Indian and Persian influences to instrumental in the founding of the Diamond Orders, and so it is unlikely that Roman mages would see every-day Vulgar Latin as holding any special standing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T17:25:09-07:00","id":1222131,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, in a Gnostic context syncretism is pretty much a given, because one of the first things one has to made peace with is that the world and all that's within are flawed because of the lie and the oppression taints everything one previously considered to be obvious. So one has both to let go and accept everything, because wisdom is something whose glimpses can only be seen by trying to look through the illusions. For someone to believe &quot;One True Way&quot; (or even a &quot;One True Destination&quot;) and trying to impose it on others because they consider it better is both a betrayal and a mistake. Since Awakening writers did their homeworks and have been getting better at it over the years, this applies to Mage too. Or Demon, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Orders work because they're a social platform that offers both infrastructure and patterns to follow, places where like-minded people can gather to try and navigate their lives as Mages, but the Awakened community as a whole mostly learned a long time ago how moot is to ascribe unmalleable wordly cultural ramification to the search for Mysteries. Dogma, even within the Pentacle, is a tool and like all tools has its uses and its dangers. I mean, if your ideals directly oppose those of, for example, the Adamantine Arrow, and nobody there believes there's potential to turn you into a passionate Arrow or has other personal reasons to want you in, then none of its members would care for you to join nor agree. You're not in the club, not interested and there's no point in wasting each other's time. Good day and good bye, try to not become an enemy of ours if possible.<br /> <br /> (The Seers play a different game, obviously)<br /> <br /> Ascension was different both because the WoD was different in background and attitude, almost everything in the setting was ruined by a variable number of jerkasses (hey, I'm saying this as someone who still loves, believes and has hope for the Garou nation, so don't sweat here) and because, while there was some Gnosticism in there, the occult practices that gave shape to it were of most often of another kind. Also because those were the 90s, with all their good and bad.<br /> <br /> But where some Mage behaviors made more sense in Ascension, they just have no place in Awakening","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-25-2018, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T18:59:36-07:00","id":1222144,"title":"","content":"What Raz, Cinder, Hermit, and Gwyn said.<br /> <br /> Diamond mages in the Roman Empire were largely bound up in the Mystery Cults that syncretised external and ancient elements into Roman culture. Thinking of Rome as analogue to Atlantis was something medieval and later European mages did. Much as the Romans themselves had a hard on for the mysterious Etruscans, and would be baffled by the image of the glorious civilisation 17th century englishmen had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:37:03-07:00","id":1222245,"title":"","content":"I think one area of confusion is reading the corebook description of Awakened society under the Diamond, and then assuming that the Diamond was always like that. That's just as fallacious as reading a description of modern English society, and then assuming that what you read also holds true for 15th century English society. Societies are never, EVER, standing still. Society IS movement of ideas. Societies are in a constant state of flux and dialogue, both internal and external. Even those that are geographically isolated to extremes (and Scandinavia was never THAT isolated) are in a constant internal dialogue, which brings about change. <br /> <br /> The Diamond orders weren't really born in a century and then already had all the names and precepts described in the corebook. It's doubtful that they were even 'born' like that at all, in the same way that you can't point to a single inarguable point at which the Eastern Roman Empire became the Byzantine Empire. Later scholars point at earlier versions of their society and say &quot;these two stages are different&quot;, but that doesn't mean they can point to a single difference. They CONSTRUCT the difference in their pointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:42:50-07:00","id":1222246,"title":"","content":"I think the other issue here is that the first edition of Mage from the outset presented the Orders as monolithic entities that had run concurrently from Atlantis until the modern day. This was changed and given more nuance later in first edition and isn\u2019t a thing at all in second. However, some people still think of them as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:38:52-07:00","id":1339087,"title":"","content":"I've done a lot of thinking and work against this question for my main homegame setting, the greater Southwest (Chihuahuan Desert to Pacific Ocean, Southern Rockies to the Sierra Madre). I've come to work with the Hellenic origins of the Diamond as an introduction of colonialism. The pre-colonial Mages had some similar orders without a major distinction between the Diamond and the Seers, seeing both as a part of an important tension in their societies - think of how Changeling Courts cede responsibility over phenomena or periods of time to each other. In thinking about greater North America, many of these mages either worked their way into the Hellenic-descended Diamond or Eurasian Seers following 1492 but many also resisted inclusion until the late-eighteenth century when the first stirrings of what would become the Nameless movement began. Pontiac's War, the Haitian Revolution, and the struggle against Spain in Mexico and Central America all represented moments where Indigenous mages worked to define themselves in concert with or against the Diamond and eventual Pentacle. The creation of independent nation-states like the USA and Mexico on the continent resulted in new Seer and Pentacle arrays in conversation with national institutions.<br /> <br /> I'm running a Mage game set in 1850 Los Angeles currently, and since Los Angeles is not a major area of interest for the U.S., other than cattle ranching, the U.S. Seers and Diamond orders mainly overlook the area. This does two things - explains the strength of the Los Angeles Free Council assembly in the future and allows me to draw an Indigenous-displaced Mexican citizen mage hierarchical order where the orders act a little differently. The closest the are has to a hierarch is a Thyrsus Guardian of the Veil named Julian Chavez, a descendant of enslaved native people from Abiquiu, New Mexico whose shadow name is Ocotillo. Chavez follows the general eschatological/messianic religion of the Guardians, but adapted to conditions where forms of magic remained more accessible and a part of everyday life (not necessarily awakened magic). Ocotillo serves as a prophet and a operations giver to other mages in the area, putting them through a crucible of physical and environmental struggle, mystery solving, and pilgrimages in the Los Angeles area and greater regions to make them more worthy of the supernal and burn away their fallen world weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25371-elzopilote","name":"elzopilote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}